// NARDOK, who sells the bone weapons the quest keeps talking about (custom, 2026-11-24).
//
// WHY HE EXISTS AT ALL. Wanted!'s third clue is "A spear, and it is made of BONE. Nobody sells
// those. Somebody down a hole carved it." - one of the three clues Old School fixes, so the spear
// itself is authentic. A player read it, went looking for the bone weapon shop he knew from Old
// School, and found nothing: this build had the weapons and no one to buy them from. The clue was
// pointing at a place the game did not have.
//
// AND HE IS PERIOD-CORRECT, which is why he is a shop and not a reworded clue. Nardok's Bone
// Weapons opened on 21 June 2006, inside this build's era, in the Dorgesh-Kaan mine, behind The
// Lost Tribe. Every one of those three facts already holds here: the mine is built and populated,
// The Lost Tribe is playable, and Wanted! REQUIRES The Lost Tribe - so nobody can reach this clue
// without already being able to reach him.
//
// NOT IN THE 377 CACHE, so he is authored from nothing the way [cave_goblin_guard1] beside him is,
// on the plain cave goblin's mesh and recolours. He takes no Attack option: he is a shopkeeper in
// a city of his own people, and the miners either side of him are the ones who fight.
[nardok]
name=Nardok
desc=He sells weapons carved from bone.
model1=npc_1822
model2=npc_1822i2
model3=npc_1822i3
model4=npc_1822i4
recol1s=6337
recol1d=7361
recol2s=4289
recol2d=5313
readyanim=cave_goblin_ready
walkanim=cave_goblin_walk
op1=Talk-to
op3=Trade
head1=npc_1822_head
vislevel=hide
wanderrange=0
